// PORT-PENDING 0092 crates-jet-foundation-src-registry-slice-1: crates/jet-foundation/src/Registry.rs:1-1808
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! D-META-REG1=A: one registration table.
//RS //!
//RS //! A marker rule, a knowledge plane, a right, and a build fact are rows of the
//RS //! same table, separated only by what they attach to. Reflection, `jet explain`,
//RS //! and the drift guards are written once here and serve all four kinds; nothing
//RS //! downstream keeps a second table or a second guard per kind.
//RS //!
//RS //! D-FACT-LAW1=B puts the law on the row itself. A fact moves toward safety
//RS //! silently; every move away is one written word at the site. So every row
//RS //! states its safe direction and the gate words that move it the other way. A
//RS //! row with no meaningful direction states `None` and names no gate;
//RS //! `law_violations` fails a row that states one without the other.
//RS //!
//RS //! D-FACT-OWN1=A adds one row shape for a fact a prover publishes. The
//RS //! ownership prover is never a plane: it publishes sendability, view
//RS //! provenance, and moved-ness as read-only rows with no plane algebra, so tools
//RS //! and other planes read them like any other fact.
//RS //!
//RS //! D-ONCE-LAW1=A adds the fifth use of the same table: a truth the compiler's
//RS //! own corpus states once. Such a row names its home, everything that renders
//RS //! the truth from that home, and the guard that proves no second copy exists.
//RS //! A registered row with no guard fails `law_violations`, which is the one
//RS //! lint the whole table shares — there is no second guard engine.
//RS 
